      "title": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $D$ is upper triangular: **false**. The entry in row 2, column 1 is $-3\\ne 0$, below the main diagonal.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $D$ is lower triangular: **true**. All entries above the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **true**. All entries below the main diagonal are zero.\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/id": "51cecce1-094a-5438-898e-ac5066c88048",
